cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper."
title: "phdid: Partial Homogeneity in Staggered Difference-in-Differences"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ronwag2005/phdid"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wagle
    given-names: Rohan
    affiliation: "Department of Economics, Ashoka University"
  - family-names: Arora
    given-names: Parush
    affiliation: "Department of Economics, Ashoka University"
abstract: >-
  Estimation and specification testing for staggered difference-in-differences
  designs under partial homogeneity of the cohort-time average treatment
  effects. Implements a Dirichlet Process mixture estimator via a collapsed
  Gibbs sampler and an l0-penalised partial-homogeneity estimator, together
  with specification tests for recoverable heterogeneity and sampler
  diagnostics including exact partition enumeration.
keywords:
  - difference-in-differences
  - staggered treatment
  - treatment effect heterogeneity
  - Dirichlet process
  - model selection
  - causal inference
  - econometrics
references:
